content":"Stout"},{"table_id":"99","column_id":"4","row_id":"6","attributes":{"border":false},"classes":"","content":"5"},{"table_id":"99","column_id":"5","row_id":"6","attributes":{"border":false},"classes":"","content":"I tried to distinguish from alcoholic version. This is smooth and creamy with that fresh taste that is what I think of when I think Guinness. It may be a bit different, but I\u2019d need a blind tasting to really determine if it is identical"},{"table_id":"99","column_id":"1","row_id":"7","attributes":{"border":false},"classes":"","content":"Wine"},{"table_id":"99","column_id":"2","row_id":"7","attributes":{"border":false},"classes":"","content":"St. Regis"},{"table_id":"99","column_id":"3","row_id":"7","attributes":{"border":false},"classes":"","content":"Chardonnay"},{"table_id":"99","column_id":"4","row_id":"7","attributes":{"border":false},"classes":"","content":"2.5"},{"table_id":"99","column_id":"5","row_id":"7","attributes":{"border":false},"classes":"","content":"It wants to be wine. Good on the tongue but a bit sweet. More similar to a Reisling, and better with food than just drinking socially."},{"table_id":"99","column_id":"1","row_id":"8","attributes":{"border":false},"classes":"","content":"Wine"},{"table_id":"99","column_id":"2","row_id":"8","attributes":{"border":false},"classes":"","content":"Ariel"},{"table_id":"99","column_id":"3","row_id":"8","attributes":{"border":false},"classes":"","content":"Chardonnay"},{"table_id":"99","column_id":"4","row_id":"8","attributes":{"border":false},"classes":"","content":"1.5"},{"table_id":"99","column_id":"5","row_id":"8","attributes":{"border":false},"classes":"","content":"Nose is decent but the wine itself tastes watery and a bit off. Doesn\u2019t really taste much like wine. Only drink while eating."},{"table_id":"99","column_id":"1","row_id":"9","attributes":{"border":false},"classes":"","content":"Wine"},{"table_id":"99","column_id":"2","row_id":"9","attributes":{"border":false},"classes":"","content":"Ariel"},{"table_id":"99","column_id":"3","row_id":"9","attributes":{"border":false},"classes":"","content":"Cabernet"},{"table_id":"99","column_id":"4","row_id":"9","attributes":{"border":false},"classes":"","content":"0.5"},{"table_id":"99","column_id":"5","row_id":"9","attributes":{"border":false},"classes":"","content":"The nose smells like wine. That is about all I\u2019ll give it. If you\u2019re going to drink it, do so with food. It was very watery, but not grape juice sweet, I found that my bottle formed some clots. Very troubling on the tongue."},{"table_id":"99","column_id":"1","row_id":"10","attributes":{"border":false},"classes":"","content":"Beer"},{"table_id":"99","column_id":"2","row_id":"10","attributes":{"border":false},"classes":"","content":"Flying Dog"},{"table_id":"99","column_id":"3","row_id":"10","attributes":{"border":false},"classes":"","content":"Deep Fake IPA"},{"table_id":"99","column_id":"4","row_id":"10","attributes":{"border":false},"classes":"","content":"3.5"},{"table_id":"99","column_id":"5","row_id":"10","attributes":{"border":false},"classes":"","content":"This brew has all of the hallmarks of an IPA, but is what I expect an \u201cIPA Light\u201d might taste like. Sound like an oxymoron? Yeah, to me too. And that\u2019s the thing about it. This brew has the bitter hoppy last I expect, and it\u2019s actually pretty good.it also tastes like beer rather than hoppy flavored water. However, its kind of thin. Is it good enough to drink if you want an IPA taste, sans alcohol. However, nobody who likes IPA and is fine with the alcohol will ever pick this over the real thing.<br><br>Perhaps I\u2019m spoiled by other non-alcoholic beer (although non of which are IPA in style) that tastes just like the real thing. It isn\u2019t bad, its just not particularly good."}]}}
